WEBVTT

00:01:27.788 --> 00:01:30.246
While these functions
are essential to our survival,

00:01:30.288 --> 00:01:32.246
we need to compensate for the fluid loss.

00:01:32.288 --> 00:01:34.538
Maintaining a balanced 
water level is essential

00:01:34.579 --> 00:01:37.663
to avoid dehydration or over-hydration,

00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:41.871
both of which can have devastating
effects on overall health.

00:01:41.913 --> 00:01:44.246
At first detection of low water levels,

00:01:44.288 --> 00:01:47.246
sensory receptors
in the brain's hypothalamus

00:01:47.288 --> 00:01:51.371
signal the release
of antidiuretic hormone.

00:01:51.413 --> 00:01:54.246
When it reached the kidneys,
it creates aquaporins,

00:01:54.288 --> 00:01:58.038
special channels that enable blood
to absorb and retain more water,

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:01.621
leading to concentrated, dark urine.